column40:
The standard example is:<p><pre><code>    void f(int x);
    void f(char *x);
    ...
    f(0);  // calls void f(int)
</code></pre>
That may seem contrived, but you may not know of the f(int) overload, especially in combination with templates.<p>NULL, if #define'd as (void *)0, prevents that error.
